WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:19.500
Good morning, Hank. It's Thursday. Hank, I just got to my hotel room in

00:00:19.509 --> 00:00:21.640
Kalamazoo Michigan and you know what was

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.840
waiting for me here?

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.410
Strawberry Hill, Peeps, and Nerds.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:28.329
Thanks Kalamazoo. And all evening long

00:00:28.329 --> 00:00:30.220
I've been thinking to myself what is it

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.320
that America wants to see me do with

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.760
Nerds, Peeps and a bottle of Strawberry Hill?

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.480
And then I realized: what America

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.280
wants to know is whether or not a Peep will

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.560
float in a glass of Strawberry Hill.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:44.920
Will it float? It floats.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.350
Look, it's a little ducky on a pink pond!

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.720
So there you have it, Hank. Peeps float in

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.750
Strawberry Hill. But wait, you say, do

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:54.850
Nerds? Hank, as you can see I have a lot

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:58.030
of grape Nerds and now we are going to

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:03.340
test them. Mmm, that looks delicious.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:07.160
Well, Hank. The answer is that Nerds

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.899
do not float except for the lone Nerd that

00:01:10.899 --> 00:01:15.580
attached itself to the Peep. Smart Nerd.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.350
Hank, many people say that Brotherhood 2.0

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:19.180
is not educational, but I would

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.370
argue that it is educational, because now

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:22.690
we've all learned an important lesson,

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:25.420
which is that if you find yourself in

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.270
the open ocean with a thousand Peeps

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:31.210
and a thousand Nerds, you should cling to

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:33.140
the Peeps and let the Nerds go.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.680
In profoundly disturbing news, it seems that

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.070
Strawberry Hill turns purple Nerds white.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:41.140
Let that be a lesson to all of you.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:42.940
If Strawberry Hill can strip purple Nerds

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:44.619
of their color, just think what it can do to

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.280
your gastrointestinal system.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.520
This is something from the comments.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:51.340
We're gonna miss you, Ze. Peter writes: "What

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.110
if your efforts to decrease suck levels

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.930
actually makes suck levels increase?
 What

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:58.360
is the contingency plan, we need an exit

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.909
strategy here". Hank, just like Peter, I'm

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:02.229
profoundly concerned that we might

00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:04.450
accidentally increase suck levels. If you

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:05.890
think about it, most of the suckiest

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:07.689
things that ever happened started with

00:02:07.689 --> 00:02:09.759
an attempt to decrease suck levels. Like,

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:11.439
for instance, you have to say that on the

00:02:11.439 --> 00:02:12.939
whole the steam engine has been a pretty

00:02:12.939 --> 00:02:16.120
good thing, but then on the other hand it

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.730
sure was warm yesterday in Colorado. But

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.650
here's the thing I'm thinking, the worst thing

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:22.900
you can possibly do is not try to

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.060
decrease suck levels. After all that's what

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.590
the first Brotherhood 2.0 book club

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:28.569
book was about. In our lifetimes we're

00:02:28.569 --> 00:02:30.459
all gonna do things that accidentally

00:02:30.459 --> 00:02:32.470
increase suck levels, but the true

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:34.689
nerdfighter is awesome enough to say: "You

00:02:34.689 --> 00:02:36.579
know what, I've made a mistake, I

00:02:36.579 --> 00:02:38.920
increased suck levels worldwide but I

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:41.530
didn't mean to. I'm sorry, and I think we

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:42.849
should change course

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:44.560
so as to decrease suck levels in the

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.379
future". Hank, that's why I'm grateful that

00:02:47.379 --> 00:02:48.939
so many people in the American

00:02:48.939 --> 00:02:51.220
government are true and awesome

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:56.769
nerdfighters. Oh, wait, crap. I'll see you

00:02:56.769 --> 00:03:00.250
tomorrow. Happy birthday to you, happy

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:05.470
birthday to you, happy birthday dear... I'm

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:11.519
gonna let Hank finish the song.

